  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Futureproof Coffee Collective Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The value chain for coffee is under pressure. Due to worldwide low coffee prices, producers do not earn a decent living income and do not have the means to establish sustainable and climate resilient production practices. Gender inequality is a persisting reality within the coffee sector and additionally, the production of coffee leads to a multitude of unaddressed and unpaid for externalities, ranging from deforestation to water pollution.This project will focus on the most stressing Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) issues in the value chain of coffee, such as underpayment, ecological degradation and gender inequality. The project partners are convinced that paying a better price to farmers is the basis for combating the above-mentioned challenges. Establishing traceable and transparent coffee value chains, enables customers and stakeholders to commit to long term solutions that incorporate social and environmental sustainability in the core processes of the value chain.Futureproof Coffee Collective Uganda is a collaboration between three Dutch coffee companies, three Ugandan value chain partners and producing organisations, one Dutch NGO and one Ugandan NGO. They will work closely with three expert organisations and one local NGO to implement the project. A larger group of companies that participate in the Futureproof Coffee Collective Uganda is ready to follow and learn from these activities in Uganda. All companies have existing sourcing relations with Ugandan partners, are keen on learning from the impact assessment and have plans for interventions in the future. This adds value for both project participants and affiliated coffee companies.</narrative>
  </description>
